# Test data: nothing under here is tracked. --test-data redirects the detector
# directories onto this folder; create it and fill it yourself (see Testing in
# the wiki). The skeleton and README that used to be tracked were a convenience,
# not a contract.
test_data/

# Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored `data/` matches at any depth and
# would also swallow 04_mc_simulation/data/ and 05_analysis_bdt/data/, which
# hold generated Monte Carlo and feature matrices — untracked for their size,
# by the *.root and *.npz rules above, not by this one.
/data/

# What the analysis concluded, not what it is: results/reco holds the
# reconstructed trees, results/plots the figures drawn from them. Both are
# rebuilt from data/ and the code whenever either changes, so tracking them put
# binary churn in every diff that touched the analysis and let the repo carry
# figures that could quietly disagree with the code beside them.
#
# 06_plots/ is now only the scripts that draw. Results do not live in a source
# folder: that is how they got committed in the first place.
/results/
